  "note": "Recorded from the hand-written pack in the commit that deleted it. Every expectation describes that pack, not the real Fly Machines API; a probe run replaces cells with observed evidence and cites the cassette.\n\nEvery step carries recorded_as: the pack named all eight operations itself and the document names them apps_list, machines_create and so on, which the receiver exports as AppsList and MachinesCreate.\n\nThe machine steps carry the id twice, as `id` and as `machine_id`. The pack read `id`; the document declares the path label `machine_id`. Neither side minds the other's spelling -- an input member no shape declares is ignored -- and writing both keeps the recording replayable against either without rewriting what the pack was asked.\n\nMachine and app ids are referenced rather than written literally, because the service issues them. The reference names `id`, not the `machine.id` the pack answered: a reference is resolved against the answer being replayed, and the document's Machine has no `machine` member to nest under. Both are hex, so unlike Hetzner's integers they unify: the comparison substitutes token-shaped strings, and every generated id here is one.\n\nWhat is still gated: the eight faults and their precedence -- a duplicate name is taken/422, a missing required member is invalid/400, an unknown app or machine is not_found/404, and a create under a missing app fails before it checks the image -- both bodyless deletes, and the whole machine list including each record's members. What is not is the four operations whose envelope the document removes.",
